    "problem_statement": "When a CPU exception is reported through the generic fault path (for example, a fault caused by an illegal instruction), the fatal error dump must include the callee-saved registers (s0 through s11) in addition to the caller-saved registers and mepc/mstatus. A panic-induced fault already lists these callee-saved registers, but a fault-induced exception currently omits them entirely, so the register dump produced for a generic CPU exception is incomplete compared to the one produced for a panic.",
